Chapter: AnnotationsSidecar
  cites Works chapter Annotation
  cites Works chapter AnnotationStore
  cites Encode chapter Json
  cites Foreword chapter Sha256
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Loads the on-disk annotation sidecars at codex.annotations/
 <chapter>.json and folds them into an AnnotationFact. Each
 sidecar is a JSON array of records:

   [
     { "target": "function:emit-start",
       "kind":   "invariant",
       "author": "cam",
       "date":   "2026-05-06",
       "body":   "...",
       "thread": null }
   ]

 The "thread" field is ignored here; threaded discussion lives
 in Discussion, not plain Annotation. Unknown kinds map to
 Discovery (the most permissive bucket).

 We say:

Section: Kind Mapping

  parse-kind : Text -> AnnotationKind
  parse-kind (k) =
    if k == "rationale" then Rationale
    else if k == "invariant" then Invariant
    else if k == "warning" then Warning
    else if k == "discovery" then Discovery
    else if k == "doctrine" then Doctrine
    else if k == "todo" then Todo
    else Discovery

Section: Date Mapping

 "YYYY-MM-DD" -> YYYYMMDD as an integer timestamp. Malformed
 dates yield 0. The format is line-based digit extraction,
 ignoring non-digits — so "2026-05-06" and "2026/05/06" both
 parse to 20260506.

  parse-date : Text -> Integer
  parse-date (s) = parse-date-loop s 0 (text-length s) 0

  parse-date-loop : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  parse-date-loop (s) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else parse-date-step s i len acc (cp-at s i)

  parse-date-step : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  parse-date-step (s) (i) (len) (acc) (cp) =
    if cp >= 48 then if cp <= 57
      then parse-date-loop s (i + 1) len (acc * 10 + (cp - 48))
      else parse-date-loop s (i + 1) len acc
    else parse-date-loop s (i + 1) len acc

  cp-at : Text, Integer -> Integer
  cp-at (s) (i) = to-unicode (char-code (char-at s i))

Section: Annotation Construction

  parse-annotation : Text, JsonValue -> Maybe Annotation
  parse-annotation (chapter) (v) = when v
    is JsonObject (pairs) -> build-annotation chapter v
    is otherwise -> None

  build-annotation : Text, JsonValue -> Maybe Annotation
  build-annotation (chapter) (v) =
    let target-str = json-get-str v "target" ""
    in let kind-str = json-get-str v "kind" ""
    in let author = json-get-str v "author" ""
    in let body = json-get-str v "body" ""
    in let date-str = json-get-str v "date" ""
    in if text-length target-str == 0 then None
    else if text-length kind-str == 0 then None
    else Just (build-annotation-record chapter target-str kind-str author body date-str)

  build-annotation-record : Text, Text, Text, Text, Text, Text -> Annotation
  build-annotation-record (chapter) (target-str) (kind-str) (author) (body) (date-str) =
    let target = AnnotationTarget { chapter = chapter, path = target-str }
    in let kind = parse-kind kind-str
    in let ts = parse-date date-str
    in let content = annotation-content-string target kind author body
    in let hash = sha256-to-hex (sha256 (text-to-bytes content))
    in Annotation { hash = hash, target = target, kind = kind, author = author, body = body, timestamp = ts }

Section: Sidecar Parsing

 parse-sidecar takes the chapter name (for the AnnotationTarget)
 and the raw JSON text. Returns a list of Annotation records;
 invalid records are silently dropped (an annotation is dropped
 if its target or kind is missing — since the system can do
 nothing useful with them — and the rest still load). Returns
 None only if the JSON itself fails to parse.

  parse-sidecar : Text, Text -> Maybe (List Annotation)
  parse-sidecar (chapter) (json-text) =
    when json-parse json-text
      is None -> None
      is Just (v) -> Just (sidecar-array-to-annotations chapter v)

  sidecar-array-to-annotations : Text, JsonValue -> List Annotation
  sidecar-array-to-annotations (chapter) (v) = when v
    is JsonArray (items) -> collect-annotations chapter items 0 (list-length items) []
    is otherwise -> []

  collect-annotations : Text, List JsonValue, Integer, Integer, List Annotation -> List Annotation
  collect-annotations (chapter) (items) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let parsed = parse-annotation chapter (list-at items i)
    in append-annotation chapter items i n acc parsed

  append-annotation : Text, List JsonValue, Integer, Integer, List Annotation, Maybe Annotation -> List Annotation
  append-annotation (chapter) (items) (i) (n) (acc) (parsed) = when parsed
    is None -> collect-annotations chapter items (i + 1) n acc
    is Just (a) -> collect-annotations chapter items (i + 1) n (list-snoc acc a)

Section: Discussion Routing

 Discussion entries in the sidecar JSON have kind "discussion"
 and carry a "thread" id. They belong in the DiscussionStore,
 not the AnnotationStore — Codex's discussion layer is a
 first-class peer of annotation, not a sub-kind. The reader
 routes them via discuss().

  is-discussion-kind : Text -> Boolean
  is-discussion-kind (k) = k == "discussion"

Section: Per-Entry Folding

 fold-sidecar-entry handles one JSON object out of the sidecar
 array. Branches on the "kind" field; routes annotations to the
 store and discussions to the thread, dropping entries that
 lack the bare-minimum fields.

  fold-sidecar-entry : AnnotationFact, Text, JsonValue -> AnnotationFact
  fold-sidecar-entry (af) (chapter) (v) = when v
    is JsonObject (pairs) -> dispatch-sidecar-entry af chapter v
    is otherwise -> af

  dispatch-sidecar-entry : AnnotationFact, Text, JsonValue -> AnnotationFact
  dispatch-sidecar-entry (af) (chapter) (v) =
    let kind-str = json-get-str v "kind" ""
    in if is-discussion-kind kind-str then fold-discussion-entry af chapter v
    else fold-annotation-entry af chapter v

  fold-annotation-entry : AnnotationFact, Text, JsonValue -> AnnotationFact
  fold-annotation-entry (af) (chapter) (v) =
    when parse-annotation chapter v
      is None -> af
      is Just (a) -> annotate-fact-with af a

  fold-discussion-entry : AnnotationFact, Text, JsonValue -> AnnotationFact
  fold-discussion-entry (af) (chapter) (v) =
    let target-str = json-get-str v "target" ""
    in let author = json-get-str v "author" ""
    in let body = json-get-str v "body" ""
    in let date-str = json-get-str v "date" ""
    in if text-length target-str == 0 then af
    else if text-length author == 0 then af
    else if text-length body == 0 then af
    else discuss af (make-target chapter target-str) author body (parse-date date-str)

Section: Folding into AnnotationFact

 load-sidecar is the convenience that takes a base AnnotationFact
 and a sidecar's chapter+text and returns the fact augmented
 with all parseable entries. A None from json-parse (JSON
 itself failed) yields the base fact unchanged. The "thread"
 id is read but the threading semantics are handled by
 Discussion (one thread per target).

  load-sidecar : AnnotationFact, Text, Text -> AnnotationFact
  load-sidecar (af) (chapter) (json-text) =
    when json-parse json-text
      is None -> af
      is Just (v) -> fold-sidecar-array af chapter v

  fold-sidecar-array : AnnotationFact, Text, JsonValue -> AnnotationFact
  fold-sidecar-array (af) (chapter) (v) = when v
    is JsonArray (items) -> fold-entries af chapter items 0 (list-length items)
    is otherwise -> af

  fold-entries : AnnotationFact, Text, List JsonValue, Integer, Integer -> AnnotationFact
  fold-entries (af) (chapter) (items) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then af
    else fold-entries (fold-sidecar-entry af chapter (list-at items i)) chapter items (i + 1) n

  annotate-fact-with : AnnotationFact, Annotation -> AnnotationFact
  annotate-fact-with (af) (a) = AnnotationFact {
    annotations = annotation-store-add (af.annotations) a,
    discussions = af.discussions,
    facts = af.facts
  }

Section: Sidecar Path Convention

 sidecar-path-for-chapter encodes the codex.annotations/...
 layout. The full path is codex.annotations/<quire>/<chapter>.json
 — but the quire prefix depends on the source's quire and the
 caller knows that better than this chapter does. So the
 builder takes both quire and chapter explicitly.

  sidecar-path-for : Text, Text -> Text
  sidecar-path-for (quire) (chapter) =
    "codex.annotations/" & quire & "/" & chapter & ".json"

